LIBPKGBUILD_EXEC_RESULT_CODEC(3)

# NAME

encode_build_execution_result, decode_build_execution_result - retain and reopen exact native build-execution evidence

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgbuild-exec/result_codec.h>*

*build_execution_result_encoding encode_build_execution_result(const build_execution_result& result);*

*build_execution_result decode_build_execution_result(const build_execution_result_encoding& encoding, pkgbuild::build_request build_request, pkgexec::execution_request execution_request, pkgexec::backend_capability_profile backend);*

# DESCRIPTION

*encode_build_execution_result*() emits the canonical versioned record for one
retained *build_execution_result*. The record embeds the canonical
*libpkgexec* execution-result encoding and retains the corresponding build
outcome, payload manifest, sealed artifact, archive-inspection receipt,
result-sealing failure, and diagnostic evidence when present.

*decode_build_execution_result*() requires the exact build request, execution
request, and backend capability profile bodies. It verifies the whole-record
checksum, delegates subordinate execution evidence to *libpkgexec*, rebuilds
payload, artifact, receipt, and build results through their public factories,
checks every retained identity, and requires canonical byte-for-byte
re-encoding.

The codec never serializes or reconstructs admitted sessions, source
materializations, package-input trees, host paths, credentials, execution
resources, or backend semantics. Identity strings are not semantic authority.
Decoding performs no source staging, program execution, payload inspection,
artifact publication, archive access, cleanup, or other mutation.

# ERRORS

Malformed, truncated, noncanonical, or internally inconsistent bytes raise
*pkgbuild_exec::error* with *corrupt_encoding*. A valid record presented with
a different build request, execution request, or backend profile raises
*authority_mismatch*. Encoding a result that violates the adapter contract
raises *inconsistent_result*.

# SEE ALSO

libpkgbuild-exec(7), pkgexec_result_codec(3), libpkgbuild(7), libpkgimage(7)
